<title>USA: ImClone Systems files for 3 mln common.</title>
<headline>ImClone Systems files for 3 mln common.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>ImClone Systems Inc filed Tuesday a shelf registration with the Securities and Exchange Commission to sell up to three million common shares.</p>
<p>After the offering, outstanding common will total 23,456,574 shares, the filing said.</p>
<p>Net proceeds will be used to continue to fund and expand its research and development programs and for general corporate purposes, including working capital.</p>
<p>ImClone, based in New York, is a biopharmaceutical company engaged primarily in the research and development of therapeutic products for the treatment of cancer and cancer-related disorders.</p>
</text>
